WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.710
The Season 2 finale of You surprised many
fans with a shocking revelation that changed

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.270
everything for Joe and Love.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:12.320
However, buried deep within the new season
is a secret second twist and hidden homicide

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.719
that only some hard-core fans have noticed.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:16.340
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.259
I'm Jan and in this video I'm revealing evidence
of a secret murder that almost everyone missed

00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:22.910
in the latest season of You.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.460
There will of course be spoilers ahead, so
take care if you're not all caught up.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.279
Season 2 surprised many viewers when they
discovered that Love is like Joe, a serial

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:35.899
killer with dangerously obsessive tendencies
who not only killed her family's au pair,

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:38.770
but also murdered Candace and Delilah.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:42.949
But there's another character whose death
remains shrouded in mystery, and that's Love's

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:44.860
late husband James.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.020
When Love tells Joe she became a widow, she
explains that her husband was ill, but is

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.239
vague on the details:
"He got sick.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:57.180
And they, um...
they tried to figure it out.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.379
But... they did not."

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:03.329
There's already something a little suspicious
about how Love mostly looks down and avoids

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.630
eye contact with Joe as she tells him this.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:10.250
But in the sixth episode we get numerous flashback
scenes that reveal a lot more about Love's

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.909
dynamic with her spouse.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:16.240
When she proposes to James that they try for
children, he doesn't seem keen on the idea.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.740
And in another flashback, he argues with Love
that they can't afford to raise children without

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:24.970
taking money from the Quinn family which is
something they'd seemingly both agreed not

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.060
to do.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.060
We can see from Love's reactions in these
scenes that James's reluctance to have children

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.880
with her was very painful, and that's also
something she alluded to while talking to

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.880
Joe.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.000
"My husband hurt me, too.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.329
Among other things, by dying."

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:42.649
Ever since she killed Sophia, Love has been
driven by a desire to create her own perfect

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:43.649
family.

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:45.390
"Families don't heal from something like that.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:48.159
So I began to fantasize about a new one."

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:52.810
But when James broke Love's heart by refusing
to have children with her, I think she plotted

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.159
to get rid of him.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:58.290
For example, just look how much Love relates
to Joe's reasons for killing Beck:

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:02.270
"Yeah, you did some terrible things but that's
what sensitive people do when they're trapped

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.439
in a bad relationship."

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:07.760
So, we have a motive for Love killing James,
but how did she do it?

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.110
Well, given she's a skilled chef, cooking
would be a likely way to put her plan into

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.110
action.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.400
And as she explained, it's also a way for
her to express her feelings.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.400
"Baking is how I express my love."

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.860
We saw how Love baked a cinnamon bun for Joe
that was made with salt rather than sugar

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.470
after she discovered he'd lied about his real
identity.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.280
At that point Love still saw potential in
Joe as a future partner and father to her

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.760
children, so she didn't full-on poison him.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.820
Instead, she made him a foul-tasting cake
as punishment and perhaps also a warning.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.970
By contrast, when James ruined Love's hope
of ever creating a family together, she probably

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:44.220
decided to really make him pay.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.590
And because Love already knew what it took
for Sophia's violent death to be covered up,

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:53.330
she may have tried to kill James in a more
subtle way that wouldn't raise as much suspicion.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:58.260
If Love found a way to poison James very slowly
so that it was hard-to-detect, then it might

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:02.190
explain the fact that nobody ever discovered
exactly what was wrong with him.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.930
In fact, she even referred to James detoxing
in one of the flashbacks.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.810
"You're just detoxing."

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.870
Which could be a wellness thing or could perhaps
hint at him having a background of alcohol

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:17.400
or drug abuse, something which would also
provide plausible cover for his becoming sick.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.650
And, of course, if there was any suspicion
by doctors or the authorities, then it wouldn't

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.560
be hard for the Quinns to cover it up, just
like they did with Sophia.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.390
Love wouldn't even need to purchase any poisons
that could be traced back to her because as

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:34.440
a chef, as well as someone heavily involved
in the wellness industry and running a grocery

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.620
store, she could well know that the seeds
of numerous fruits like apricots, cherries

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.690
and peaches naturally contain cyanide compounds.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:46.610
With Anavrin's produce and kitchen at her
disposal, Love could easily grind up small

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:51.160
amounts of fruit stones and blend the powder
in with James's meals to slowly administer

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.610
small quantities of cyanide that would make
him sick.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:58.410
Perhaps it's even a little tell that Love
uses a peach as her introduction to Joe.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.440
"Do you think this peach looks like a butt?"

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.650
And it's curious how Love reacts when Joe
is hesitant to eat the muffins she brings

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.060
him to eat while he's in the cage.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.280
"Is this what you're afraid of?

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.020
No poison, Joe!"

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:14.450
As Joe and Love are basically a mirror image
of each other, Joe might well be thinking

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:19.910
of what he did to Benji or what Love did with
the salty bun, but that moment is also drawing

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:23.680
our attention to Love's ability to poison
her victims.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.840
Ok, the poison theory may be plausible, but
you might ask why was Love so visibly upset

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.870
and angry at James for hiding the fact that
he knew about his illness for 8 weeks before

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:33.890
he told her?

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:37.351
Well, it's worth remembering that although
Love and Joe are both serial killers, they

00:04:37.351 --> 00:04:40.250
each seem to react differently when killing
someone.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:44.600
Joe seems to be much more dispassionate and
cold-blooded whether he's killing on purpose

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.000
or accidentally.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.680
But each time we've seen Love murder, whether
it be Candace, Delilah or Sophia, she's been

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.090
angry and distressed.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:57.640
So, even if Love knew she was the reason James
was unwell, she could be simultaneously upset

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.460
but determined to go through with the deed
because of her own warped obsession with raising

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:02.510
a family.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:05.610
We can see this when she explains to Joe why
she killed Delilah.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:10.910
"Did you actually believe I wanted to hurt
anyone?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.780
I hated doing that to Delilah.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:17.240
Was I gonna let this destroy our baby's life?

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.230
My whole life...

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:25.050
I've been doing what it takes...
when I love someone."

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:29.350
And all the way back in the first episode
of Season 2, Love makes an interesting connection

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.970
between the death of her husband and Joe.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.710
"Ever since it happened,
I've been able to see this thing in people...

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.110
who've been through it.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.110
I see that every time I look in your eyes."

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:42.520
Love later finds out that Joe killed Beck,
and if she sees the same in Joe as she does

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:47.430
in herself, that's a big pointer that Love
also killed the one she loved, James.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:52.781
Basically, both Joe and Love fantasise about
a perfect partner or family and when their

00:05:52.781 --> 00:05:56.840
loved one fails to fulfil that fantasy, they
kill them.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:01.130
Some fans have also tried to connect Delilah's
death with James by suggesting that she'd

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.530
begun to investigate James's death along with
Henderson's.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:08.610
They've pointed to the board of information
Delilah was using to write her article about

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:11.260
Henderson and said that there's a picture
of James on there.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.330
Now, I've checked the scene myself, and I
can't see any such picture, only a newspaper

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:19.920
cutting mentioning Henderson's cancer and
a photo of him that you could say resembles

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:20.920
James a little.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.150
There is a mention of a "James" on an article
to the side of that.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:28.420
The article's cut off, but the title seems
like it might be about a "Film Executive."

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:32.371
And it talks in the past tense about a certain
"James" who appears to have worked in the

00:06:32.371 --> 00:06:33.880
entertainment industry.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:38.130
If this is Love's deceased husband James then
it's possible she met him through Forty's

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.490
attempts to break into the movie business.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:45.190
So, given what Love probably did to her husband,
there's a chance she'll try to kill Joe as

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:49.550
well, especially if she catches him creeping
around their next-door neighbour.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.350
Maybe she'll start slipping something into
Joe's food.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:57.630
And if Joe uncovers the truth about what happened
to James, he'll very likely run for the hills.

